  {
    "episode_id": 82241,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82241.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "In his first round of interviews, since his new job was announced, John Kerry told NPR that the new administration's international work on climate change will start with rejoining the Paris Climate Agreement. He spoke to NPR as Steve Enscape. Is it simple for the United States",
