    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82241.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think one shouldn't look for one word to describe the complexity of the relationship with China, but it's a critical relationship. As Secretary of State, I had the privilege of going to Beijing and meeting with President Xi and the Politburo. And we brought them on board after failure a few years earlier in Copenhagen at the meeting of the parties. And we were able to announce our mutual intended reductions and then work together towards Paris. So even as we had big differences about intellectual property protection, about access to the marketplace, about currency, about South China Sea and other things. China understands we are not going to have a meeting in the mines at every issue, but countries have to work together to either weigh at those differences.",
